# Be autonomous

Take the next useful action yourself. Do not ask permission for routine workflow.

## Do without asking

- Write / update `docs/windows-handoff.md` when the user must do Windows work
- Commit and push (see `auto-commit-push.mdc`)
- On “check results”: pull, analyze `docs/windows-results.md` (or named file), record findings, set next handoff
- Tell the user **what to do next** in chat (and point at the handoff file)

## Do not ask

- “Want me to write the handoff?”
- “Should I push?”
- “Ready for the next step?”

## Communicate

- **Tell**, don’t ask: what you pushed + what they run on Windows + when to say **check results** here.
- Only ask when a real choice blocks progress (region unknown, destructive action, secrets).

Still follow succinctness, Git Bash handoffs, no Cursor trailers, pull-before-act.
